    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The event sequence, traceable to a verified equipment failure in Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2, triggered a data-driven escalation protocol by the grid management authority. This grid stability procedure was necessitated by a documented supply-demand imbalance caused by high demand from seasonal heat. Officials, acting as crisis decision-makers, authorized an emergency load management action, a calculated grid protection measure to prevent overloading. The consequence was a quantified power deficit, rendering more than 950 megawatts unavailable in the Visayas region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
