      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Analysis of the grid incident reveals a pattern of pre-existing generation shortfalls compounding the initial failure of the power generation unit. The system overseer responded with an automated system response, a grid stability procedure, to manage the severe generation loss. This forced demand reduction was an emergency measure, creating a significant capacity shortfall of over 950 megawatts. The sequence highlights the tension between infrastructure readiness and acute weather-driven load stress on the energy sector entity.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
