      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The documented outage of the tripped unit initiated a chain reaction, exposing the energy infrastructure to stress from an energy demand spike. Grid stability monitors executed an alert declaration, a control action, to stabilize the network. The resulting emergency measure to shed load averted a wider power outage but confirmed a substantial energy deficit. This incident serves as a factual case study in grid incident management under conditions of demand exceeding safe capacity.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
